        "answer": "c",
        "explanation": "VTY lines accept every protocol until they are restricted, and generating keys only adds SSH as an option. The transport input ssh command is what removes Telnet. A larger key changes the strength of SSH, not which protocols the lines accept. Service password-encryption only obscures stored line passwords in the configuration and does nothing about traffic on the wire. The banner delimiter is just the character that ends the banner text and has no effect on which sessions are accepted."
