        "answer": "b",
        "explanation": "A trap level sends that level and every numerically lower, more severe level. Warnings is level 4, so levels 0 to 4 are sent and levels 5 (notifications) and 6 (informational) are held back. Debugging at level 7 would send everything, including the noise the SOC wants to avoid. Errors at level 3 would drop warnings, which include failed-login messages that the SOC specifically needs. Notifications at level 5 would still include the unwanted notification messages such as configuration-change notices."
